# Cline Rules for LeechBot

## Project
Telegram file transloader bot. Pyrogram 2.0.106, Python 3.10+, asyncio.

## Before Making Changes
1. Read `AGENTS.md` for architecture overview
2. Read `ARCHITECTURE.md` for technical details
3. Check `leechbot/utility/variables.py` for existing state
4. Check `config.py` for existing configuration

## Code Conventions
- Async/await everywhere
- `logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)` at module top
- Standard file header (project, developer, GitHub, Telegram, license)
- No linter — follow existing patterns
- Import state from `variables.py`, mutate directly

## State Management
ALL mutable state lives in `leechbot/utility/variables.py`. Classes:
- `BOT.Setting` (persistent), `BOT.Options` (per-task), `BOT.Mode`, `BOT.State`
- `Queue` (download queue), `Transfer` (transfer stats), `BotStats` (cumulative)
- `Messages` (dynamic text), `MSG` (message refs), `Paths` (file paths)

## Adding Commands
1. Handler in `leechbot/commands.py` with `@app.on_message(filters.command("cmd"))`
2. Register in `__main__.py` `_register_commands()`
3. Update `GUIDE.md`

## Adding Downloaders
1. New file in `leechbot/downloader/`
2. Link detection in `leechbot/utility/helper.py`
3. Routing in `leechbot/downloader/manager.py`

## Known Issues
- `reply_media_group()` has no `progress` param — use per-photo upload + file_id
- Pyrogram 2.0.106: no `style` on `InlineKeyboardButton`
- Telegram: 2GB limit, media group max 10

## Changelog
Every change → new entry at top of `CHANGELOG.md` with Version, Date, Description.

## Testing
Test suite in `tests/`. Expand with pytest + pytest-asyncio.
